          <p>Asteroids are rocky, metallic, or carbonaceous bodies left over from the Solar System's formation 4.6 billion years ago. Most orbit in the Asteroid Belt between Mars and Jupiter. They range from tiny pebbles to the dwarf planet Ceres (940 km wide). Over one million asteroids larger than 1 km are thought to exist in the inner Solar System.</p>
